-- food: Food and Drink
DO $do$
DECLARE v_id integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE keywords[1] = 'food' ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE 'food' = ANY(keywords) ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  END IF;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "HelpEntry"
      (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file, updated_at)
    VALUES (
      ARRAY['food', 'rations', 'fountain', 'fountains']::text[],
      'Food and Drink',
      $help$Hunger and thirst show on SCORE. They do not slow healing, but they do
wear you down over time, and a full stomach is a good habit.

  eat {food}           eat bread, rations and the like
  drink {container}    drink from a waterskin, cup or flask you carry
  drink {fountain}     drink from a fountain in the room

Fountains in towns are free. Inns and general stores sell food and
drink. Torches and lanterns are sold there too: see TORCH.

See also: EAT, HUNGER, SHOPS.$help$,
      0,
      'command',
      'eat {item} | drink {item}',
      'data/help/food.md',
      now()
    );
  ELSE
    UPDATE "HelpEntry" SET
      keywords = ARRAY['food', 'rations', 'fountain', 'fountains']::text[],
      title = 'Food and Drink',
      content = $help$Hunger and thirst show on SCORE. They do not slow healing, but they do
wear you down over time, and a full stomach is a good habit.

