-- newbie: Getting Started
DO $do$
DECLARE v_id integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE keywords[1] = 'newbie' ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE 'newbie' = ANY(keywords) ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  END IF;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "HelpEntry"
      (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file, updated_at)
    VALUES (
      ARRAY['newbie', 'start', 'getting-started', 'new-player', 'beginner', 'tutorial', 'first-steps']::text[],
      'Getting Started',
      $help$Welcome to FieryMUD. These are the first steps for a new character. Type
"help {topic}" for details on anything named here.

LOOK AROUND
  look               describe the room         exits    list the exits
  north (n), south (s), east (e), west (w), up (u), down (d) move you.
  scan               peek at the rooms next to you.
  score              your stats       inventory (i)    what you carry
  equipment (eq)     what you wear    wealth           your coin

FIND YOUR WAY
  "exits" lists the exits of the room. "autoexit" shows them every
  time you look. "areas" lists the zones. The Training Academy teaches
  the basics: see ACADEMY. Shops are marked in the room list; use "list"
  inside one to see what it sells.

GEAR UP
  New characters start with a few items: check "inventory". You start
  with no coin; killing monsters drops some. wear {item}, wield {weapon},
  remove {item}, get, drop, give. A badly dressed character takes far
  more damage. Shops sell gear: see SHOPS.
  The world gets dark at night. Carry a torch ("light torch"; see
  LIGHT and TORCH) or you will see nothing until morning.

LEARN YOUR CLASS
  skills, spells and practice show what you can do. Trainers (NPCs) teach
  you and spend the practice points you earn by levelling. See SKILL and
  MAGIC. "where {name}" can help you find another player.
  Casters learn spells with "study": "study" lists the spells you can
  learn now, "study {spell}" learns one.

FIGHT SMART
  consider {target}  tells you how dangerous something is. Try it first.
  kill {target}      start a fight.          flee    run away.
  wimpy 30           flee automatically below 30 percent HP.
  rest, sleep and food and drink recover HP and stamina; "stand" gets you
  up. Check hunger and thirst on score.

STAY SAFE
  Touch a touchstone in a safe place, and "recall" will take you back to
  it from anywhere. Keep spare coin in the BANK.

PLAY WITH OTHERS
  GROUPS, CHANNELS (gossip, tell), CLANS, BOARDS and MAIL. Quests are
  listed with "quests"; see QUESTS.

SETTINGS AND ACCOUNT
  PROMPT, color, brief, alias. For passwords, the website and the
  "code" login, see WEBSITE.

Lost? "commands" lists every command, and "help" with no topic shows the
index.$help$,
      0,
      'guide',
      'newbie',
      'data/help/newbie.md',
      now()
    );
  ELSE
    UPDATE "HelpEntry" SET
      keywords = ARRAY['newbie', 'start', 'getting-started', 'new-player', 'beginner', 'tutorial', 'first-steps']::text[],
      title = 'Getting Started',
