-- study: Study
DO $do$
DECLARE v_id integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE keywords[1] = 'study' ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE 'study' = ANY(keywords) ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  END IF;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "HelpEntry"
      (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file, updated_at)
    VALUES (
      ARRAY['study', 'memorize', 'pray']::text[],
      'Study',
      $help$Casters learn their spells with STUDY. Skills come with your class as you
level and need no study.

  study              list the spells you can learn right now
  study {spell}      learn one

A spell is listed once you have reached its circle, and not before. Quest
spells are not offered. Learn one, then "spells" shows what you know and
"practice" shows how well.

Spell slots are separate. "slots" shows how many you have ready and how
long the spent ones take to recover. Slots recover on their own, faster
while you rest or meditate, so there is nothing to memorize.

See also: SPELLS, SLOTS, MAGIC, MEDITATE, PRACTICE.$help$,
      0,
      'command',
      'study | study {spell}',
      'data/help/study.md',
      now()
    );
  ELSE
    UPDATE "HelpEntry" SET
      keywords = ARRAY['study', 'memorize', 'pray']::text[],
      title = 'Study',
      content = $help$Casters learn their spells with STUDY. Skills come with your class as you
level and need no study.

  study              list the spells you can learn right now
  study {spell}      learn one

A spell is listed once you have reached its circle, and not before. Quest
spells are not offered. Learn one, then "spells" shows what you know and
"practice" shows how well.

Spell slots are separate. "slots" shows how many you have ready and how
